    thinking: "**Designing Interactive Widgets**\n\nI\'m excited! The interactive visualization widgets are taking shape. To make my projects section stand out, I\'m now exploring custom UI simulation components. The goal is to provide users with hands-on interaction with mock datasets, offering a breathtaking glimpse into each project\'s potential. I\'m wondering where to begin with the design!\n\n\n**Organizing Simulator Components**\n\nI\'ve decided to keep the simulator components clean by creating `/src/components/ProjectSimulators/` for modularity and performance. Each simulator, like the Sales Dashboard Simulator, will feature filters and animated KPI cards for interaction. I\'ll use CSS to create beautiful and fast interactive charts, specifically vertical flex layouts with animated bars representing \"Ventas por Mes,\" leveraging SVG polygons or bars for custom styling.\n\n\n**Defining Simulator Inputs**\n\nI\'m now outlining specific interactive elements for the simulators. For the Churn Predictor, there\'ll be sliders for customer attributes and a risk gauge. The B2B Lead Scoring simulator will utilize sliders, checkboxes, and dynamic score tiers. Each simulator design is beginning to be outlined now.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/components/ProjectSimulator.tsx` containing five interactive widgets corresponding to our five data projects. Each will serve as a mini, live analytical playground that hiring managers can test in real-time. This provides realistic interactive data computations, showing SQL-like aggregation reasoning in standard React code."
