    thinking: "**Defining App State**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the core state needed for `App.tsx`. I\'ve outlined the essentials: a category for filtering projects (with options like \'All\', \'Sales\', etc.), and an ID to manage the interactive demo display, probably using `null` to indicate no demo is active. This will allow for instant simulator mounting.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Set**\n\nI\'m now expanding the feature set. I\'ve considered an accordion or detail card to showcase project details, ensuring recruiters stay engaged. I\'m also planning the form state for the contact section, including inputs, sending status, and custom log execution simulation. Additionally, I\'m working on dark mode implementation with Tailwind\'s `dark` class, and a sticky nav with section buttons and a theme toggler. I\'m also working on refining the Hero Section.\n\n\n**Designing Hero Section**\n\nMy current focus is on the Hero Section, envisioning a \"Senior Data & Product Analyst\" title in a petroleum blue accent. I\'m incorporating dual actions: \"Ver Proyectos Anal\303\255ticos,\" triggering a smooth scroll, and \"Descargar CV,\" which will activate an options modal for CV download, a fast text summary, or a custom print. On the right, I\'ll mount the `DataConstellation` interactive SVG network chart for visual impact.\n\n\n**Refining Project Section**\n\nI\'m now refining the \"Proyectos\" section. I\'m focusing on dynamic category selector tabs with animated underlines and seamlessly filtered project lists. Each project card will showcase a custom infographic, title, category, subtitle, description, tech badges, and an impact highlight. Crucially, each card will include a button to view an interactive demo (with a simulator toggler) and a GitHub button.\n\n\n\n**Structuring Experience Data**\n\nNow, I\'m structuring the Experience section as a timeline. Hovering over each block will highlight it and display role, company, and duration, along with bullet points. I\'m excited to include a miniature \"M\303\251tricas Clave Movidas\" indicator with rounded badges showing key metrics like \"+9.3% Conversi\303\263n Onboarding.\" I\'m also planning the Education and Certifications sections, with a structured layout dividing academics from certifications, including issuer stamps and credential links.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now implement a functional, accessible, and responsive user experience in `/src/App.tsx`. It features:\n1. **Dynamic Theme Switching** between Light & Dark modes, adjusting the custom palette seamlessly.\n2. **Interactive Project Filter** that segments projects by category.\n3. **Live Analytical Simulators Inline** allowing users to click \"Ver Demo de Anal\303\255tica\" to toggle the responsive widgets directly under the project description.\n4. **Interactive Timeline** highlighting key KPI changes made at previous jobs.\n5. **Themed Contact Form** with a live SQL transaction simulator.\n6. **Detailed Resume Viewer Overlay** to inspect and export Matteo\'s profile.\n\nI will write `/src/App.tsx` now."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 607149444
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
