h existing design patterns. The cards are great, so no major issues there!\n\n\n**Integrating Brand Styling**\n\nI\'m now integrating the \"Bold Typography\" theme by focusing on branding. I\'m taking cues from the Design HTML, specifically the header navigation, and I\'m looking at how `JA.ANALYTICS` and similar branding elements are styled. I will check the navigation bar logo in `src/App.tsx`. I want to achieve a visually striking brand identifier, something like `MATEO.ANALYTICS` in bold, tracking-tight uppercase.\n\n\n**Refining Menu Styling**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the top menu branding and navigation links in `src/App.tsx`. I\'ve updated the brand logo to reflect the design, using the branding from JA.ANALYTICS as a guide, and now render the logo with an elegant style, using Mateo\'s name. I updated the navigation links, and I\'m very happy with the results.\n\n\n**Adjusting Layout Structures**\n\nI\'m now integrating hero section styling, as found in `src/App.tsx`. I\'ve updated the top menu branding. I\'m focusing on the `Hero` layout, and the `Hero` section styling. I\'m adapting the grid and flex structure to incorporate bold typography as defined in the Design HTML, specifically the headings, the font size, and the letter-spacing as it applies to the `Hero` sections. I am also making sure the overall look and feel matches the brand. I\'ll make sure the left-hand text has the styles from Design HTML.\n\n\n**Implementing Hero Styling**\n\nI\'m now integrating hero section styling, as found in `src/App.tsx`. I\'ve updated the `Hero` section to adapt the grid and flex structure to incorporate bold typography as defined in the Design HTML. I have implemented a multi-line title with appropriate spacing and updated subtitle and paragraph styles to align with the design spec. I am pleased with the results, and will proceed to integrate the changes into the layout. I\'m taking cues from the old layout now.\n\n\n**Styling Hero Section Buttons**\n\nI\'m now styling the call-to-action buttons within the `Hero` section. I\'m focusing on their visual appeal and hover states. I\'ve updated the styles for the \"Download CV\" and \"Contact Me\" buttons in `src/App.tsx` based on the Design HTML to match their intended looks. I am pleased with the results, and will move to integrate these changes into the overall layout.\n\n\n"
